THOUGHT: NullAway reports `this.allTiles` as nullable at the dereference `this.allTiles.get(id)`. Even though there is an explicit null check just above, NullAway may not be smart enough to infer non-null after the compound condition. A simple, safe fix is to store `this.allTiles` in a local variable after the null/size checks and use that local for the `get` call; this often helps NullAway understand the flow. I’ll modify the method accordingly and then run the build to confirm the error count decreases by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '270,284s/return this.allTiles.get(id);/    List<ITilesetEntry> tiles = this.allTiles;
    if (tiles == null) {
      return null;
    }

    return tiles.get(id);/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/tilemap/xml/Tileset.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error\\(s\\)" new_build_output.log | tail -n 20
```

